.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Staging documents, deliberately untracked. Globs, not filenames: a
# convention protected one name at a time will eventually miss one, and the
# miss is silent -- an untracked staging file is one `git add -A` from being
# committed, which is exactly what the convention exists to prevent.
*-STAGING.md
DRAFT-ISSUE-*.md

# Named, not globbed: `*-PLAN.md` would swallow REFACTOR-PLAN.md, which is
# tracked. This file is a working document whose name follows REFACTOR-PLAN.md
# rather than the -STAGING.md convention it documents.
STAGING-SKILL-PLAN.md

# Staging archive. Spent staging files are moved here, never deleted — the
# register in tmp/archive/<date>/README.md says what became of each. Ignored
# because the staging convention above is "uncommitted by design", and an
# archived file must not become committed by being archived.
tmp/
